place UT_JumpPuzzle_LiftMechanism_Lever bridgelever at 10 -42.5 ground sit yaw=90
# the outpost's map screen
place RT_RadarScreen mapscreen at 6.5 -8.5 ground sit yaw=200
# the climb: a mountain (trail winding up from bearing 250), a 10-storey climbing tower on its top, the summit box
call vd_mount x=55 z=25 top=22 r=20 a0=250 turns=1.25 hb=3
call vd_tower x=55 z=25 h0=22 lv=10 a=dltw box=dlbox zal=dltopz zid=dl_top msg="The timber port's crane. The jib still points at the river mouth; the route strongbox sits out on its end."
note dlbox Crane cab box | RIVER PEOPLE - TIMBER PORT. Logs came down the upper river and swung out to the barges from here. The strongbox on the jib keeps the route.
loot dlbox Rope*3;Plank*4;Bolt*2
# the crane's jib: two floor tiles out east from the deck, the route strongbox (a keypad) at its end
place Block_Floor_Tier3 dljib at 57.25 24.25 h={22+10*2.42+0.215}
place Block_Floor_Tier3 dljib at 58.75 24.25 h={22+10*2.42+0.215}
prop dljib tint.color=#6e6a64
prop dljib tint.amount=0.55
# (box agent 10-25: 0.07 m into the jib tile - raised)
place RT_PowerBox cranepad at 59.2 24.25 h={22+10*2.42+0.50} yaw=270
# the dive: BoatStranded on the sea floor 10 m down, its crate, an air pocket
call vd_dive x=-12 z=-98 h=-10 yaw=30 obj="BoatStranded" al=dlwreck crate=dlcrate zal=dlwz zid=dl_wreck msg="The timber barge, down on the river's silt fan. A fuse box is bolted to its wheelhouse." air=dlair bub=dlbub
note dlcrate Barge's fuse box | A ranger fuse for the mouth relay, wrapped in oilcloth. Somebody meant to come back for it.
loot dlcrate story:fuse*1;Scrap*3;Rope*1
# the gorge hill north-west: a fisher's lookout on top (secret)
call vd_mount x=-48 z=40 top=16 r=18 a0=120 turns=1 n=40 hb=3
place Loot_ChestSmall dllook at -48 40 h=16 sit yaw=200
note dllook Lookout box | A fisher's spyglass box. Scratched inside the lid: THE BARGE LIES WHERE THE PUFFERS FEED.
loot dllook Rope*2;Scrap*2;Leather*1
prop dllook loot.refill=0
call vd_spot x=-48 z=41.5 al=dllookz id=dl_lookout r=3 msg="From the gorge hill the three arms shine like a hand laid on the jungle."
call ni8cave x=-59 z=10 h=2 yaw=180 al=dlottercave
place Loot_ChestSmall dlottercavebox at -56.5 5 h=2.45 sit yaw=200
place Placeable_Lantern_Metal - at -61.6 6 h=2.45 sit
note dlottercavebox Otter den stash | The river people kept their spare net and a jar of something strong here.
loot dlottercavebox Rope*2;Leather*2;Coconut*2
prop dlottercavebox loot.refill=0
call vinecache x=30 z=55 r=7 seed=11331 chest=dlvine vines=dlvinevines items=Bolt*2;Nail*6;Plank*3
prop dlvine note.title=Vine-choked crate
place Creature_Llama dlllama at 34 60 ground
prop dlllama creature.count=2
call treasure x=-44 z=-40 r=8 n=1 seed=11380 kind=0
prop treasure11380 treasure.loot=Scrap*6;Bolt*3;Nail*10

# --- STORY 10-24: Teodor's water trial at the map screen, Hedda's ferry log, the fisher's diary, Pim's note in the otter den
beside Note_Paper teodortrial mapscreen d=1.4
note teodortrial Water trial, sheet 1 | SEEDKEEPERS - HEART LAB - WATER TRIAL, SHEET 1 - T. LIND\n\nSite: river people's outpost, Riverfork Delta.\nProblem: brown foam on the stones, fish belly-up in the drawbridge arm, children with rashes. Old oil in the silt from the timber barges.\n\nTrial: one dose of V-1 in the outpost's water barrel. V-1 is a spore that eats oil and gives back clean water and flowers. Nothing else. I have checked it two hundred times.\n\nDay 1: foam gone.\nDay 3: the drawbridge arm runs clear. Hedda says the water tastes sweet. Children say it tastes like sweets.\nDay 6: vines on the ferry rope. Small. Lovely, really.\n\nI am so happy I could cry. I will tell Marit tonight. She said I would never fix the river. I have fixed the river.
# (REACH 10-28: at 0.3 over the ground it lay in the bank - dropped from 1 m)
place Note_Paper ferrylog at -18.5 5 ground y=1.0 drop
note ferrylog Ferry log | FERRY LOG - HEDDA, ferry keeper\n\nCrossings today: 31. Fares paid: 4. Fares paid in fish: 9. Fares paid in "I will pay you tomorrow, Hedda": everyone else, as usual.\n\nThe rope is growing leaves. I cut them in the morning and by supper there are more. The lab man says it is good. The lab man has never had to wind a ferry with a salad on the rope.\n\nThe water smells sweet at night. People go down to the bank and stand there, just stand. Old Ulf stood there till midnight and said he heard singing upriver.\n\nI told him that was the boars. He did not laugh. He always laughs at my jokes; that is why he pays in fish.
place Note_Paper fishernote at 28 -16 ground y=0.3 drop
note fishernote Fisher's diary | ULF - FISHING, drawbridge arm\n\nThe puffers have come back to the barge wreck. They feed where it lies, off the mouth, ten metres down. I have not seen puffers here since I was a boy.\n\nThe fish taste of honey now. My wife says that is not natural. I say nothing about this river has been natural since the timber men came. This is the first nice thing.\n\nThere is singing upriver at night. Not people. More like a lot of leaves moving the same way at the same time.\n\nTomorrow the whole village is going up to see. Hedda says she is staying with the ferry. Hedda says that every time, and then she comes.
place Note_Paper pimnote at -57.8 6.5 h=2.5 drop
note pimnote Note in the otter den | MY HIDING PLACE, by PIM (age 9). KEEP OUT. EXCEPT OTTERS.\n\nEveryone is walking upriver to the singing. Mum said come on Pim. I said no because I am hiding, and you do not stop hiding just because people want you to.\n\nThe otter lets me sit here if I give her my fish. I have given her all my fish.\n\nIf the ranger lady comes: I did NOT take the apples. The otter took the apples. Also I took some apples.\n\nIt is very quiet now. I think I will go and find mum after all. The singing sounds nice.\n\nPim

# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest ----------------------------------------------------------------
info title=Riverfork Delta
info author=Custom Islands
info description=A jungle delta cut by river arms: the river people's outpost, vines on the paths, a rope ferry and boars upriver. The third island of The Last Green World.
island on.arrive=message||Fresh water runs into the sea here - three river arms through the jungle. Somewhere a wheel creaks on a rope.

story ferry|Ferry crossed|Note_Paper|The delta's rope ferry, wound across the ferry arm.

note riverchart River chart | THE DELTA - RIVER PEOPLE'S CHART\n\nWest arm: the ferry. Keep the vines cut.\nEast arm: shallow, no crossing in rain.\nUpper river: the fuel cache and the pressing shed. Boars.\nOutpost: tools on the rack.\n\nUpriver of everything: the rise, and past it the hollow trees.
note rangerlog4 Ranger log 4 | RANGER LOG 4 - O. FENN\n\nThe river people are gone. Their shed is full, their fire cold, their pot of porridge still on the hook. Fourteen people do not leave porridge. Hedda would come back from the dead for porridge.\n\nIn their water barrel I found a little glass vial, empty, with a lab label: V-1 - T.L. - TRIAL DOSE. Teodor's writing. He told me once the delta water was the worst on the coast. Now it is clear as glass, and it smells of flowers, and nobody is here to drink it.\n\nI have the vial in my breast pocket. I will ask him what it is. I will ask him very calmly.\n\nThe boars charged me twice today. The animals turn mean near the dark roots. I am going up onto Tracker's Rise - the trackers' tower can see the whole wood, and the trackers can see where fourteen people walk to.
note toolrack Outpost tool rack | The outpost's tool rack: a machete's plans pinned beside an empty hook.
note fuelcache Fuel cache | The river people's fuel cache: plans for a fuel tank and its pipes, in a tin box.
note pressshed Pressing shed | The pressing shed's chest: the press's plans, explosive goo in a jar and a sack of potatoes.
loot toolrack Blueprint_Machete*1;Machete*1;Rope*2;Nail*8
prop toolrack loot.refill=0
loot fuelcache Blueprint_Fueltank*1;Blueprint_Pipe_Fuel*1;MetalIngot*2;story:fuelcan*1
prop fuelcache loot.refill=0
loot pressshed Blueprint_BiofuelExtractor*1;ExplosiveGoo*2;Raw_Potato*3
prop pressshed loot.refill=0
prop pressshed obj.name=pressshed
prop pressshed beh.hidden=1
story fuelcan|Fuel can|Placeable_FuelTank|A dented can of the river people's fuel. The press takes three.
story pressed|Press running|Placeable_FuelTank|The pressing shed's press runs again; its door is open.
note dcanwest West bank can | A fuel can wedged under the ferry landing, in a small chest.
loot dcanwest story:fuelcan*1;Rope*2
prop dcanwest loot.refill=0
note dcaneast Fisher's can | The fisher's camp kept a can by the fire, behind the vines that grew over it.
loot dcaneast story:fuelcan*1;Raw_Herring*2;Leather*1
prop dcaneast loot.refill=0
prop dcaneast obj.name=dcaneast
prop dcaneast beh.hidden=1
prop eastvines obj.name=eastvines
prop eastvines on.use=hide|\nshow|dcaneast\nmessage||The vines come away. A fisher's camp, and a fuel can by the cold fire.
prop shedvines obj.name=shedvines
prop shedvines on.use=hide|\nshow|press\nmessage||Behind the vines: the river people's press, dry as a bone.
prop press obj.name=press
prop press beh.hidden=1
prop press beh.use=Fill the press
prop press if.use=take|story:fuelcan|3
prop press on.use=message||Three cans in. The press coughs, catches and thumps; the shed's bar drops off its door.\ngive||story:pressed*1\nshow|pressshed
prop press else.use=message||The press needs fuel: three cans. The river people kept one on each arm.
prop dhatch obj.name=dhatch
prop dhatch on.use=hide|\nshow|dhatchchest\nmessage||Under the hatch: the river people's spirit store.
note dhatchchest Spirit store | The river people's spirit store, dug into the dune: their good tools and a river pearl.
loot dhatchchest MetalIngot*3;Bolt*4;Hinge*2;Placeable_GiantClam*1;Seed_Mango*2
prop dhatchchest loot.refill=0
prop dhatchchest obj.name=dhatchchest
prop dhatchchest beh.hidden=1

prop westvines obj.name=westvines
prop westvines on.use=hide|\nmessage||The vines part under the machete. The path runs down to the rope ferry.
prop ferrycrank beh.use=Wind the ferry across
prop ferrycrank if.use=!signal|ferry
prop ferrycrank on.use=signal||ferry\ngive||story:ferry*1\nmessage||The rope tightens and the ferry crawls across the river, bumping the far bank.
prop ferrycrank else.use=message||The ferry is across.

prop mouthzone zone.id=mouth
prop mouthzone zone.radius=6
prop mouthzone zone.message=The river mouth. Fresh water and salt water swirl together over the sand.
prop westarm zone.id=west_arm
prop westarm zone.radius=3
prop westarm zone.message=The ferry arm. A rope ferry, a crank wheel on a post.
prop upriverzone zone.id=upriver
prop upriverzone zone.radius=6
prop upriverzone zone.message=Upriver. A fuel cache, a pressing shed - and boars.

# DEEP 10-24 settings
story fuse|Relay fuse|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|A ranger fuse for Relay Mouth, from the sunk barge.
story relay|Relay switched on|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|One of the delta's three ranger relays, humming again.
story rivercode|Route code|Note_Paper|The map screen's code: 4172.
story route|River route|Note_Paper|The river people's route through the delta to the rise.
note forksign Fork sign | RANGER RELAYS\n\nRELAY NORTH - up the river, past the cross, behind the bad vines.\nRELAY EAST - over the drawbridge. Lever on this side.\nRELAY MOUTH - by the landing. Its fuse went down with the barge.\n\nAll three on: the outpost's screen shows the route.
